# Protection boundary for the unattended nightly automation (2026-07-18 portfolio
# audit): the files below decide WHAT the agents may write and WHICH sources are
# authoritative. Ownership here is declarative until a branch ruleset requires
# code-owner review — enable that under Settings → Rules if/when the repo gains
# other contributors. The nightly publish job never touches these paths (it stages
# only data/ dist/ and skill logs), so this boundary is also enforced structurally.

# CI / automation definitions and the supply-chain pins they rely on
/.github/ @riles22
/requirements.txt @riles22

# Semantic registries: which sources exist, how tiers normalize, what a refresh owes
/data/sources.json @riles22
/data/scales.json @riles22
/data/required-sources.json @riles22
/data/community.json @riles22
# The three remaining Gate-0 immutable paths (audit 2026-08-14 — this list named two of the
# five that nightly.yml's boundary guard actually protects, so the declared boundary was
# narrower than the enforced one). season-final.json is written ONLY by the deterministic
# freeze step; forecasts/ holds the immutable artifact the report card grades; season-archive/
# renders verbatim as a public page. All three are append-only and unrecoverable if rewritten.
/data/season-final.json @riles22
/data/forecasts/ @riles22
/data/season-archive/ @riles22
# Applied into community.json at prebuild, so it is a registry edit by another route
# (audit 2026-07-24, A2 — Gate 0 now applies it before its own boundary diff).
/data/community-overrides.json @riles22

# The deterministic gatekeepers themselves
/src/validate.mjs @riles22
/src/check-refresh.mjs @riles22
/src/check-skill-logs.mjs @riles22
/src/apply-ratings.mjs @riles22
/src/apply-metrics.mjs @riles22
# The freeze lane writes the two append-only records above, so it belongs with the
# gatekeepers rather than with ordinary source (audit 2026-08-14).
/src/freeze-season.mjs @riles22
/src/freeze-season-archive.mjs @riles22
# normalize.mjs holds PHASES — the single era vocabulary the whole season transition turns
# on — and render.mjs holds SNAPSHOT_PHASE, PHASE_FLIP_DUE and the frozen projection weights
# that CLAUDE.md says may be tuned "in code only". Both are one edit away from moving every
# published letter, which is the same reason the registries above are listed.
/src/normalize.mjs @riles22
/src/render.mjs @riles22
# LF pins that keep the built artifacts' CSP hashes matchable and the flip patch byte-exact.
/.gitattributes @riles22
# The agent lane's test reporter (2026-08-15 context audit). No gate uses it — every
# deterministic gate keeps the default reporter — but it is what an agent reads a red
# suite through, so a change here changes what the automation believes about its own tests.
/src/quiet-reporter.mjs @riles22
